# Driver Inattention Detection – Deep Learning Project

This is a course project for the Deep Learning class at Tilburg University (Spring 2025).  
The objective was to develop an image classification model using convolutional neural networks (CNN) to detect six types of driver inattention behaviors (e.g., yawning, sleepy driving, drinking, etc.).

## My Contribution

I was responsible for the model optimization phase, including:

- Performing hyperparameter tuning (optimizer, dropout rate, number of neurons, filter size, etc.)
- Training and evaluating models using the university's GPU4EDU platform
- Comparing performance across model variations using ROC curve, AUC, and confusion matrix
- Preparing results for handoff to teammates and integration into the final report

## Tools & Frameworks

- Python  
- TensorFlow / Keras  
- Google Colab  
- GPU4EDU  
- Matplotlib

## Outcome

The improved model achieved higher classification accuracy and better balance across classes than the baseline, demonstrating the impact of tuning key architectural parameters.
